==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[præeminent]] {{qualifier|18 <sup>th</sup> century}}
* [[pre-eminent]]
* [[preëminent]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|preeminent|lang=fr}} and its source, {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|praeēminēns|lang=la}}, present participle of {{term|praeeminere|praeēminēre|to stand out, excel}}, from {{term|prae-||pre-}} + {{term|eminere|ēminēre}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/pɹiːˈɛmɪnənt/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Exceeding others in quality or rank; of outstanding [[excellence]], extremely [[notable]] or [[important]]. {{defdate|from 15th c.}}

====Derived terms====
* [[preeminence]]
* [[preeminently]]

